        "NURSING CARE": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "NURSING CARE",
          "canonical_heading": "NURSING CARE",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Restricted activity combined with physical therapy—may help neurologically disabled patients in the postoperative period; a cart may be necessary for severely affected patients.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Management of urination—essential for cases in which disorders of micturition accompany the spinal injury.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "ACTIVITY": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "ACTIVITY",
          "canonical_heading": "ACTIVITY",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Restricted, especially if vertebral subluxation is present.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "DIET": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "DIET",
          "canonical_heading": "DIET",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Maintaining a lean bodyweight limits stress on the spinal column.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "CLIENT EDUCATION": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "CLIENT EDUCATION",
          "canonical_heading": "CLIENT EDUCATION",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Many congenital vertebral malformations are clinically silent.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Perform a thorough workup when a congenial malformation results in neurologic abnormalities.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Heritability is suspected; avoid breeding.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Many neurologically affected dogs and cats left untreated are euthanized.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Early surgical intervention often necessary to alleviate compression of the spinal cord and prevent further damage.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "In general, surgical decompression is required when congenital malformation(s) cause narrowing of the spinal canal and compression of the spinal cord. In cases of chronic or diffuse spinal cord compression, improvement following surgery is minimal.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Atlantoaxial subluxation—surgical ventral decompression combined with stabilization of the atlantoaxial joint with pins or screws is the treatment of choice.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Spina bifida—meningoceles can be closed surgically to prevent leakage of cerebrospinal fluid and infections; surgery usually not attempted when the spinal cord parenchyma is involved.",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Spina bifida associated with spinal cord malformation, chronic neurologic disease despite surgical treatment, and lower motor",
              "pdf_page": 396,
              "printed_page": 314,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
